WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.682 --> 00:00:04.022
Eh, quick one. You got a list with 5 bus stops:

2
00:00:04.042 --> 00:00:07.542
Harbour, Market, Library, Park, Zoo.

3
00:00:07.562 --> 00:00:09.832
You ask Python for stop number 5.

4
00:00:10.729 --> 00:00:13.302
Python crash, sia! IndexError.

5
00:00:13.322 --> 00:00:17.032
How come? Got 5 stops, but where got index 5?

6
00:00:17.322 --> 00:00:19.649
Today we settle list basics lah.

7
00:00:19.669 --> 00:00:22.102
How to take 1 item with an index.

8
00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:25.222
How to count from the BACK with a negative index.

9
00:00:25.242 --> 00:00:26.862
How to cut a slice.

10
00:00:26.882 --> 00:00:31.062
Then len, and in, and 4 methods that change the list:

11
00:00:31.082 --> 00:00:33.902
append, insert, pop, remove.

12
00:00:33.922 --> 00:00:36.582
Small topic, but the exam love it one.

13
00:00:36.602 --> 00:00:39.382
After this, you can trace a list question by hand, no

14
00:00:39.402 --> 00:00:41.172
need to anyhow guess.

15
00:00:43.165 --> 00:00:45.785
So this list ah, we call it stops.

16
00:00:45.805 --> 00:00:49.055
Python start counting at 0, NOT at 1.

17
00:00:49.085 --> 00:00:52.545
Step 1: stops at index 0 is Harbour.

18
00:00:52.565 --> 00:00:56.265
Step 2: len of stops is 5, so the last index

19
00:00:56.285 --> 00:00:58.505
is 4, that one the Zoo.

20
00:00:58.525 --> 00:01:01.469
Index 5? Don't have, so crash lor.

21
00:01:01.489 --> 00:01:05.149
Step 3, the shortcut: stops at minus 1.

22
00:01:05.169 --> 00:01:08.909
Negative index count from the back, so minus 1 is ALWAYS

23
00:01:08.929 --> 00:01:12.059
the last item. Zoo already, no need len.

24
00:01:12.089 --> 00:01:15.429
Now the slice: stops, 1 colon 3.

25
00:01:15.449 --> 00:01:17.389
You get Market and Library only.

26
00:01:17.409 --> 00:01:20.829
Why ah? Because the slice start AT index 1 and stop

27
00:01:20.849 --> 00:01:25.389
BEFORE index 3. So 3 minus 1, that is 2 items.

28
00:01:25.409 --> 00:01:28.509
Leave out the start, stops colon 2, you get the first

29
00:01:28.529 --> 00:01:32.189
2 stops. Leave out the end, stops 3 colon, you get

30
00:01:32.209 --> 00:01:36.349
Park and Zoo. And a slice very relaxed one: stops 3

31
00:01:36.369 --> 00:01:39.899
colon 99 still give Park and Zoo, no crash.

32
00:01:40.119 --> 00:01:44.510
The trap: people count 1, 2, 3 and write 3 stops.

33
00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:47.790
Wrong leh! And a slice give you a NEW list, the

34
00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:49.660
old list never change.

35
00:01:51.745 --> 00:01:53.645
Next, the word in.

36
00:01:53.665 --> 00:01:55.645
Park in stops? True.

37
00:01:55.665 --> 00:01:57.565
But park with small p?

38
00:01:57.585 --> 00:02:00.355
False lah, must match EXACTLY.

39
00:02:00.529 --> 00:02:01.965
Now the 4 methods.

40
00:02:01.985 --> 00:02:04.205
All of them change the list itself.

41
00:02:04.225 --> 00:02:08.325
Start with 3 stops: Harbour, Market, Library.

42
00:02:08.345 --> 00:02:11.805
Append Zoo: Zoo go to the END, like joining the hawker

43
00:02:11.825 --> 00:02:17.485
queue. Insert 1, School: School take index 1, everybody behind shift

44
00:02:17.505 --> 00:02:21.565
1 place. Pop 0: take out Harbour AND give it back

45
00:02:21.585 --> 00:02:25.765
to you. Remove Library: find that VALUE, take it out.

46
00:02:25.785 --> 00:02:28.275
Left with School, Market, Zoo.

47
00:02:28.295 --> 00:02:30.125
Why got 2 ways to take out ah?

48
00:02:30.145 --> 00:02:33.925
Because pop use the POSITION, remove use the value.

49
00:02:33.945 --> 00:02:37.725
And if the value not inside, remove give you ValueError, so

50
00:02:37.745 --> 00:02:39.155
check with in first.

51
00:02:39.825 --> 00:02:45.325
Then the trap, sibei common: stops equals stops dot append Airport.

52
00:02:45.345 --> 00:02:46.235
Alamak!

53
00:02:46.305 --> 00:02:49.995
Append return None, so now your whole list become None.

54
00:02:50.065 --> 00:02:51.115
Gone already.

55
00:02:51.345 --> 00:02:54.875
Just write stops dot append on its own line, can already.

56
00:02:56.867 --> 00:03:02.367
Okay, the one-line takeaway: index start at 0, slice stop BEFORE

57
00:03:02.387 --> 00:03:06.437
the stop value, and append change the list but return None.

58
00:03:06.467 --> 00:03:10.087
Only pop hand something back: the item it took out.

59
00:03:10.107 --> 00:03:13.087
Remember these hor, then most list questions you can trace by

60
00:03:13.107 --> 00:03:14.077
hand already.

61
00:03:14.291 --> 00:03:16.087
Now go do the practice notebook.

62
00:03:16.107 --> 00:03:20.047
Got 6 exercises, all about bus routes: 2 to predict, 2

63
00:03:20.067 --> 00:03:22.567
fix the bug, 2 write from scratch.

64
00:03:22.587 --> 00:03:25.047
Got a function there that keep asking for a stop that

65
00:03:25.067 --> 00:03:27.597
does not exist, you go catch it.

66
00:03:27.671 --> 00:03:31.251
Last thing: graded work must be your OWN, the course does

67
00:03:31.271 --> 00:03:32.851
not allow AI on it.

68
00:03:32.871 --> 00:03:36.584
So practise here until steady, then that one you do yourself.

69
00:03:36.604 --> 00:03:37.441
Jia you!
